78:## Acceptance criteria / deterministic matrix
79:
80:- [ ] LIB-01 empty active Library shows Father-facing empty state and `Criar novo catálogo`.
81:- [ ] LIB-02 metadata listing performs no full `CatalogDocument` fetch per row.
82:- [ ] LIB-03 default view is active-only.
83:- [ ] LIB-04 archived view is separate.
84:- [ ] LIB-05 title search works deterministically.
85:- [ ] LIB-06 ordering is deterministic, recently updated first by default with useful title ordering available.
86:- [ ] LIB-07 blank create uses fresh lowercase UUID-compatible root identity, valid canonical document, authoritative create ACK, then ordinary exact route open.
87:- [ ] LIB-08 Open uses exact catalog ID and the W3.C/W3.D bootstrap pipeline.
88:- [ ] LIB-09 missing catalog has no first/nearest/title fallback.
89:- [ ] LIB-10 Rename uses canonical `document.rename`, complete snapshot Save/CAS, and projection changes only after ACK.
90:- [ ] LIB-11 stale Rename fails closed on revision conflict.
91:- [ ] LIB-12 failed Rename does not create Library-only title authority.
92:- [ ] LIB-13 Archive requires explicit confirmation.
93:- [ ] LIB-14 successful Archive removes from active and appears in archived view.
94:- [ ] LIB-15 stale Archive conflicts/fails closed.
95:- [ ] LIB-16 stale pre-archive Save cannot resurrect an archived catalog.
96:- [ ] LIB-17 stale pre-archive Rename cannot resurrect an archived catalog.
97:- [ ] LIB-18 stale open tab cannot ordinary Save or implicitly unarchive after Archive.
98:- [ ] LIB-19 Library Open preserves W3.D Recovery startup gate before authoring.
99:- [ ] LIB-20 Library navigation/archive does not delete unrelated Recovery records.
100:- [ ] LIB-21 unauthorized Library row/action fails closed.
101:- [ ] LIB-22 Duplicate cloning is not implemented in W3.E.
102:- [ ] LIB-23 no hard Delete exists.
103:- [ ] LIB-24 no Restore/Unarchive contract is invented.
104:
105:## Father UX
106:
107:- Heading: `Catálogos`
108:- Primary action: `Novo catálogo`
109:- Search: `Buscar catálogos`
110:- Views: `Ativos` / `Arquivados`
111:- Active actions: `Abrir`, `Renomear`, `Arquivar`
112:- Duplicate may be shown only disabled with clear future capability semantics.
113:- Archive copy explains that the catalog leaves the active list and is not permanently deleted.
114:- Errors distinguish not found, unauthorized, offline, remote failure, conflict, and invalid document in Father language.
115:- No revision, mutation, CAS, database, JSON, Git, or Recovery-internal terminology is exposed.
116:
117:## Mobile / accessibility
118:
119:- 320–390 px widths must have no horizontal overflow.
120:- Search, active/archived switch, create, row actions, rename dialog, and archive confirmation remain touch-usable.
121:- Keyboard focus is visible and dialogs expose accessible labels/titles.
122:- Desktop remains a compact professional library rather than a generic card wall.
123:
124:## Stop conditions / known boundary
125:
126:- If blank creation cannot use the canonical factory, stop for Principal decision.
127:- No cross-tab dirty-state discovery is invented. Same-tab navigation away from dirty editor work must be guarded. A separate stale editor tab is protected by existing CAS/archived server semantics: after another surface archives or renames, stale Save/Rename must fail closed rather than silently overwrite/recreate.
128:- Recovery records are never broadly deleted by Library operations.
129:- No W3.F identity clone logic may enter this branch.
130:
